+## 3 Complete the legal and privacy engineering
+
+Use existing privacy/community services and platform boundaries. Implement a versioned general-terms record distinct from the current community-rules acceptance. Preserve the exact version/hash, locale, acceptance time and account binding with minimal evidence. Offer a readable/saveable copy before agreement, before paid checkout and at relevant account/publication boundaries. An unchecked explicit action must not double as optional analytics or ad consent. Terms changes must respect existing purchases and any notice/termination requirements; do not silently invalidate old purchases or receipts.
+
+Retain local/offline play and its existing recovery semantics while any general licence acceptance is presented at an appropriate boundary. A pending network response must not delete saves, purchases or authored files. Terms refusal and account deletion are distinct choices. Migration policy must explicitly cover existing accounts and historical purchases rather than invent consent.
+
+Implement the public-track policy as checklist LCP-40. Present section 7's purposes, continuing licence, creator immutability/no hiding, deletion consequences and exact slot charge before publication. Prevent owner replacement/revision/hiding through UI, API, queued commits and older clients; allow a changed layout only as a deliberately separate track publication. Preserve acknowledged exact retries, slot accounting and a versioned account-bound licence record. The current community agreement grants narrower permissions: assess actual prior grants, obtain valid fresh agreement where needed, and keep legacy uses within existing rights until resolved. Do not silently rewrite old acceptance records or condition unrelated existing paid rights on an unnecessary broader grant. Keep statutory removal/retrieval and identifying-data handling available. Publisher compatibility derivatives must follow immutable content/race versions rather than overwrite pinned evidence. Current confirmation copy and source gaps are in the [publisher decision record](PUBLISHER_DECISIONS_2026_10_25.md).
