+LCP-39 now implements the selected distinction: uninstallation retains the account and its unexpired benefits; deliberate, informed deletion of the entire account ends them without a new-account grant or automatic refund solely for deletion. Prominently warn about all affected paid time before confirmation and preserve mandatory claims. Do not condition erasure on purchase-dispute resolution or resurrect identity/progress/benefits from caches/backups. No explicit blanket transfer requirement after voluntary deletion was found in the checked Google rules; the earlier automatic-restoration recommendation is not treated as a binding requirement. A store purchase record or already-owned response is a technical/provider state to handle separately, not proof of entitlement on a replacement game account. Preserve lawful minimum records and required remedies; the [publisher decision record](PUBLISHER_DECISIONS_2026_10_25.md) records the interpretation, evidence and acceptance cases. This is a selected draft policy subject to normal regional/provider review, not a legal certification for every transaction.
