+# Publisher decisions — 25 October 2026
+
+This records the publisher's ten answers and subsequent decision to replace permanent ad-free with twelve months paid once without automatic renewal. The current [terms are revision 6](TERMS_DRAFT.md). It supersedes the permanent-product and automatic new-account restoration proposals. The [revision-4 baseline](../evidence/launch-compliance-2026-10-24/terms-before-publisher-decisions.txt) and [revision-5 baseline before the annual decision](../evidence/launch-compliance-2026-10-24/terms-before-annual-ad-free.txt) are retained. These are draft-policy decisions, not effective player agreements or implemented runtime changes.
+
+| Answer | Decision and status | Draft or implementation consequence |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| 1. Initial free slot | **Confirmed:** one initial free publishing slot. The publisher intends a small publication cost to discourage misuse/bad content. Extra slots as race rewards are a **possible future option**, not an approved reward schedule. | Section 8 has no monthly allowance. Describe any actual reward eligibility before offering it; grant verified awards once without creating a recurring promise. Payment does not exempt content from moderation or guarantee quality. |
+| 2. Published tracks | **Confirmed:** the creator cannot change or delete a published track, because other game features rely on it. | Sections 7–8 prohibit creator replacement, revision, hiding and withdrawal. A changed layout may be published as a separate track using another slot where offered. Preserve pinned race/rivalry/challenge identities. Necessary publisher moderation/privacy/legal removal and separately versioned compatibility adaptations remain, alongside the previously requested gameplay-change rights. |
+| 3. Notice | **Confirmed:** at least 60 days' advance notice, announced in game, for planned global or regional discontinuation. | Section 14 now contains that commitment. Implement a persistent dated notice with territorial/feature scope and accessible retained copy. Provide any additional legally required form/longer notice. The existing urgent legal/security exception remains; ordinary cost or profitability decisions are not automatically emergencies. |
