+# Beat my track terms and conditions draft
+
+**Draft for publisher and Finnish legal review. Not effective or published.**
+
+Proposed version: `bmt-terms-draft-2026-10-24`. Effective date: **[TO BE SET AFTER REVIEW]**.
+
+These terms govern personal use of Beat my track, including the game, online racing, track creation and sharing, and purchases offered by its publisher. They explain the service limits, player responsibilities and remedies that apply when something goes wrong.
+
+## 1 Publisher and contact
+
+The publisher and contracting party is **[LEGAL PUBLISHER NAME]**, established in **[COUNTRY]**, business registration number **[NUMBER OR NOT APPLICABLE]**, business/contact address **[PUBLIC ADDRESS]**. In these terms, “we”, “us” and “our” mean that publisher.
+
+Contact support and complaints at **[SUPPORT EMAIL]**, privacy matters at **[PRIVACY EMAIL]**, security reports at **[SECURITY EMAIL]**, and illegal-content notices at **[PUBLIC NOTICE URL OR EMAIL]**. These contacts may use the same monitored mailbox. Authority contact and supported languages: **[AUTHORITY CONTACT AND LANGUAGES]**.
+
+The official legal information page is **[LEGAL PAGE URL]**. Our privacy notice is **[PRIVACY URL]**, community rules are **[COMMUNITY RULES URL]**, and external account-deletion resource is **[ACCOUNT DELETION URL]**.
+
+## 2 Your agreement and mandatory rights
+
+You must have a reasonable opportunity to read and save these terms before agreeing to them. The purchase description and checkout information form part of the agreement for that purchase. The community rules also apply when you publish or interact with public content. The privacy notice explains processing of personal data; accepting these terms does not provide consent for optional analytics or advertising.
+
+Nothing in these terms removes or restricts rights or remedies that applicable law makes mandatory, including rights concerning delivery, defective digital content or services, refunds, personal data and access to courts or competent authorities. Those rights prevail over any inconsistent clause.
+
+## 3 Age and eligibility
+
+**[INSERT APPROVED MINIMUM AGE, INTENDED AUDIENCE, COUNTRY VARIATIONS AND ANY PARENTAL AUTHORISATION PROCESS BEFORE PUBLICATION.]**
+
+Where parental or guardian authorisation is legally required, it must be obtained through the applicable process. A content rating describes content suitability and does not replace requirements concerning contractual capacity or personal-data consent.
+
+## 4 Licence and service requirements
+
+We give you a personal, non-exclusive licence to install and use the game for its intended purposes, subject to these terms and applicable store conditions. We and our licensors retain ownership of the game and its assets. Third-party software and assets remain subject to their applicable licence notices; these terms do not restrict rights those licences or mandatory law give you.
+
+The store listing states supported devices, operating systems and relevant requirements. Online accounts, public publication and verified competition require a compatible connection and service version. Local/offline features work only where the installed version and available local content support them. We do not promise every online feature works offline or on every device.
+
+Ordinary racing is not subject to a paid retry or energy requirement. Optional purchases do not buy competitive vehicle performance. A publishing purchase does not charge recipients for ordinary racing on the shared track.
+
+## 5 Accounts and local files
+
+Use the sign-in process honestly and keep access to your identity provider secure. Tell us if you reasonably suspect account misuse. You are responsible for your own conduct, but these terms do not make you automatically responsible for every unauthorised action by someone else.
+
+Keep a backup of valuable local drafts using the available save/export facilities. Account sign-in does not imply that every local record, draft or setting is stored online. Account and purchase recovery depend on the relevant account and provider records. We will apply reasonable security and recovery measures required by law; this section does not exclude liability for our own failure to do so.
+
+## 6 Fair play and verification
+
+Do not submit fabricated results, manipulate race evidence or purchase records, exploit security weaknesses to obtain an unfair advantage, impersonate others, or deliberately disrupt the service. Activities permitted by mandatory law, including applicable interoperability and research rights, remain permitted.
+
+Competition results are subject to the published race rules, the relevant content and rules version, and evidence checks. We may investigate, temporarily hold, reject or correct a result when there are reasonable grounds to consider it invalid. Changes to handling or rules may create separate competition records instead of converting historical records. A purchase does not guarantee a finishing position, matchmaking outcome, ranking, reward eligibility or prize.
+
+Actions affecting an account or published content follow section 11. We do not promise the service will prevent every cheat or that every suspected result will be resolved immediately.
+
+## 7 Your tracks and other public content
+
+You retain your rights in content you create. Only upload content you have the right to share. Do not include another person's protected work, confidential information or personal data without an appropriate right or legal basis. Follow the community rules for track designs, names, challenge titles and car appearances.
+
+When you deliberately publish content, you grant us a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free licence to host, reproduce, technically adapt, display and distribute that content as reasonably needed to operate the game, including previews, downloads, moderation and compatibility processing. We may permit our service providers to perform those tasks on our behalf. This licence may pass to a successor operating the game as described in section 19, subject to the same purposes, limits and applicable rights. It does not transfer ownership of your content or give us a general right to sell it for unrelated uses or use it to train AI models.
+
+Other players may download and use deliberately shared tracks in the game. Previously downloaded copies may remain after public removal. Any continued use or retention following deletion, withdrawal or termination is subject to applicable law, including personal-data rights and any mandatory rights concerning content you supplied. A content licence does not waive those rights.
+
+## 8 Purchases and entitlements
+
+Only products actually available in the release store may be purchased. The checkout identifies the seller/payment provider, product, total price, duration and relevant conditions. Prices and currency must agree with the payment provider's checkout. A simulation or test transaction is not a paid purchase.
+
+Purchases attach to the game account identified before checkout. Check that account before confirming. Recovery restores the entitlement or remaining account balance supported by the verified transaction; it does not grant the original product a second time. Pending, cancelled or unverified transactions do not confer an entitlement. Contact support if a confirmed payment is not delivered.
+
+The five currently proposed product types are:
+
+| Product | Scope to be confirmed in the final product description |
+| --- | --- |
+| 1 publishing slot | One additional publishing allocation under the disclosed allocation, replacement and retirement rules. |
+| 5 publishing slots | Five additional allocations under those same disclosed rules. |
+| 10 publishing slots | Ten additional allocations under those same disclosed rules. |
+| One month ad-free | One calendar month of the advertised ad-free benefit. It is a one-time purchase, not an automatically renewing subscription. Further purchases extend the benefit from the later of its expiry or purchase time. |
+| Permanent ad-free | A non-expiring account entitlement to the advertised ad-free benefit while the service is supplied. It does not promise perpetual operation or continued maintenance. Online services may end for the reasons in section 14. Any later discontinuation remains subject to the purchase agreement and mandatory remedies. |
+
+**[BEFORE SALES: DEFINE WHICH AD FORMATS EACH AD-FREE PRODUCT SUPPRESSES, HOW REWARDED RESUMES WORK, HOW A SLOT IS ALLOCATED/REUSED, AND THE EFFECT OF HIDING, WITHDRAWING OR MODERATING A TRACK.]**
+
+Earned Coins, racing points and other non-cash game balances have no cash redemption or transfer function offered by us. This does not remove any statutory refund or compensation right. We do not sell performance advantages, Coins or XP under these product terms.
+
+## 9 Withdrawal, refunds and defective purchases
+
+Applicable consumer withdrawal rights and remedies remain available. A statement that an item is digital, consumed or non-refundable does not itself remove those rights. Where the law allows loss of a digital-content withdrawal right after immediate supply, the required prior express consent, acknowledgement and durable confirmation must be obtained through the relevant checkout process. Digital services may have different rules.
+
+Use the applicable store refund process or contact **[SUPPORT EMAIL]** with the order reference and problem. For contracts with a continuing withdrawal right, the required withdrawal function is **[WITHDRAWAL URL OR APPROVED PROVIDER FLOW]**. You may also send a clear withdrawal request using the available contact details. We will explain the applicable remedy and repayment process.
+
